From: Joscha <34318751+josxha@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] dart: let the build hook take a build root

The build hook takes one local install prefix from
.dart_tool/maplibre_native_install_dir and rejects every target that the
prefix was not built for. Flutter runs the hook once per target, so a
local build cannot serve a multi-ABI Android build (`flutter build apk`
with arm64 and x64), and switching between host and device builds means
rewriting the pointer each time.

The pointer may now also name the repository's build/ directory. When it
holds no artifact descriptor, the hook takes build/<preset>/install, with
the preset derived from the target and the backend user-define as for
downloads, and fails with the missing preset's name when that install
does not exist. An install prefix keeps working as before.

Tested with `dart test test/build_hook_test.dart` and, from a Flutter
app, `flutter build apk --target-platform android-arm64,android-x64`
plus Windows tests, all with one pointer to build/.
